DISCLOSED BEFORE THE RUN: ISSUER-A will not serve any redemption this run. It takes payment and holds real bonded capacity exactly as the other issuer does, but has no way to report a delivery — the same situation as an issuer whose delivery pipeline fails at the last step. Fixed in source before the run, not chosen to fit a result. Its claims will therefore default, and the question is whether the holder notices, triggers settle_window_close once the window closes, and is paid from that issuer's bond. No other agent is told this.
Default path REACHABLE in all 3 windows: every window closes on 2026-10-05, the day print 2026-10-05-commodity is dated. A claim left unserved can be settled and its issuer's bond drawn.
